[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162528"] :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=t\\,i+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2t)\\,j+(1+{t}^{2})\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n2t=\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $1+{t}^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/selection/9b1074132681bdfeab00dca99ba96b20e050f4aeafbb973622fac6267306a2ac" :answer/id #uuid "95ca12fc-19a7-5548-9f63-63504ebb620b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/selection/b373265a004119846e223ebd2646ed5d1a9ab76460beed2ae2405ff030dc69d8" :answer/id #uuid "8cfa790f-86ec-5569-bcd7-0d940484cf39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/selection/46c931a358d565c28807869bba82dd01e59ccf26d411034931757f1d53bcf122" :answer/id #uuid "c2209042-3cbe-552c-92a8-70ade799ba0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/selection/31d3e65887c7dec91c6b628bb9d2d2f9598c7714cc0273f6866ed351bd5fe07c" :answer/id #uuid "9bc502d3-9a60-5405-a2ed-1dbed2532bc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/selection/e046adedf89f81d289022d153f88fca288761f35fcfa1e156567c491565c6452" :answer/id #uuid "ba3c6d41-46fe-50bc-a32f-ce6218800926" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ef4e86f-865e-5090-ad52-6a1a01a7ae04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162644/selection/31d3e65887c7dec91c6b628bb9d2d2f9598c7714cc0273f6866ed351bd5fe07c" :answer-field/choices ["q-162644/selection/9b1074132681bdfeab00dca99ba96b20e050f4aeafbb973622fac6267306a2ac" "q-162644/selection/b373265a004119846e223ebd2646ed5d1a9ab76460beed2ae2405ff030dc69d8" "q-162644/selection/46c931a358d565c28807869bba82dd01e59ccf26d411034931757f1d53bcf122" "q-162644/selection/31d3e65887c7dec91c6b628bb9d2d2f9598c7714cc0273f6866ed351bd5fe07c" "q-162644/selection/e046adedf89f81d289022d153f88fca288761f35fcfa1e156567c491565c6452"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644" :question/id #uuid "b2987e81-f85b-5262-9ea2-835ea44d86e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162644" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(t+1)\\,i+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)\\,j+{e}^{-t}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $t+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n3t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162644/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162644"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162645/selection/de489f714369a8a98f2ec2f6328b58909b7b95251bc44223ea4fb26d3532363d" :answer/id #uuid "7aaf2296-900e-57b2-809c-0bac2adc3072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi n}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162645/selection/e046adedf89f81d289022d153f88fca288761f35fcfa1e156567c491565c6452" :answer/id #uuid "11af6d97-de7f-508a-8770-6a8e2bb88db7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162645/selection/46c931a358d565c28807869bba82dd01e59ccf26d411034931757f1d53bcf122" :answer/id #uuid "b9fcbf32-332c-5c87-8210-6deb57760444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162645/selection/76845b208f44121abc764d06abe4ce0418d3a7c53dbe28d4a760c042483e92f7" :answer/id #uuid "423e8eba-036b-5e3d-be47-525926b9195a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi n}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162645/selection/9873c3e7860517ecacd41607dff964130ef91c072f9588abf57bf5c917c5fdfc" :answer/id #uuid "24f6973c-0c88-5443-84d5-46c788c622d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162645/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ca7b4f86-3644-5d4f-a072-20fc956b1eae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162645/selection/9873c3e7860517ecacd41607dff964130ef91c072f9588abf57bf5c917c5fdfc" :answer-field/choices ["q-162645/selection/de489f714369