valued function $f(s)=⟨\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-s),\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\sqrt{s}$ is $s\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-s)$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,2).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{3}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064302/assets/808abeaa59d7bcea3b24e741fde5296791de32b4170d60f05f2a5af203c20ba2.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is $s\\in [0,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162659/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a1499c-080d-5008-bcc3-492ef469d3dc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162659"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162662/selection/370dac9d03449729e49b15f1af1eb04a59ec2d35e23f36d49bf428e7bf3363d3" :answer/id #uuid "02b53821-b1a8-50a5-84c3-5382be015953" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [0,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162662/selection/16422adcf80007a50c56bcc46245c56657afa3ccddfc62c0d5cb1e7e38ac5920" :answer/id #uuid "e48c0f48-3647-507b-861d-b0f368770723" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162662/selection/efb15a9436b44d061d2d7649239083e2e5384b3f9a5d46689b1880c71625545a" :answer/id #uuid "3365dd4b-c122-5005-bac4-d8965a752fd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-1,0)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162662/selection/ccd67e015b54478fe66dc2403e4e966af6e63b9b96cee55decd748dc4ea2a406" :answer/id #uuid "2c430095-8a84-5a0b-a79b-b5d6417d3262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :an